Crypt::Age::Header::parse_from_fh is a public method with no =method block, while every other public method in the module has one. It came in with the filehandle-first rewrite (PR #3) and is the entry point Header::parse delegates to, so a caller working with filehandles has nothing to read.

Should document: what it consumes from the handle, that the handle is left positioned at the first payload byte, that it captures the literal header bytes for the MAC, and which malformed inputs it dies on (now including the X25519 stanza rules from karr #5).

Found while reviewing karr #5. Doc-only, no behaviour change - crypt-age-doc-writer.
